  "179:93": {
    "inputs": {
      "text": "Five-second continuous shot. Begin from the supplied composite image and its original mascot placement. After a brief pause, Todeok takes two short, relaxed steps toward the camera along the right-side pedestrian deck, alternating the feet at an even pace, then settles with both feet side by side. Both legs use equal stride lengths and equal low foot clearance. During each step, the supporting foot stays planted while the other foot lifts, moves forward and lands. The torso stays balanced with minimal side-to-side sway. Keep the original facing direction.\n\nKeep the original white 3D mascot design, face, body proportions and smooth surfaces. Both wings remain rounded, solid, fingerless flippers. The balloon-holding wing keeps the same closed grip relative to the torso throughout; the free wing rests beside the body. The four original colored balloons stay attached to the same strings and follow the motion with only a slight delayed sway. Keep their count, shapes and colors consistent.\n\nSmooth slow dolly-out at eye level: the camera gently pulls back along the bridge at the same pace as the mascot walks forward, keeping it at about the same size and position in the frame with the balloons fully visible, while the steel truss beams and railings on both sides glide slowly toward the camera, deepening the tunnel-like perspective. Stay on the right-side pedestrian deck, parallel to the rails and clear of the railing. The railbike is parked and completely still for the entire shot: it does not move forward or backward, its wheels do not turn, and the two riders stay seated in the same pose. Preserve the bridge beams, rails and perspective. Keep consistent lighting throughout.",
      "clip": [
        "179:84",
        0
      ]
    },
    "class_type": "CLIPTextEncode",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "CLIP Text Encode (Positive Prompt)",
      "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
      "ver": "0.3.45"
    }
  },
